# Offline LAN = one local server (do not regress)

Canonical: `docs/DESIGN.md` § DeviceSetup Server Mode · `docs/DEV.md` § Branches offline · vision §5.

## Offline (cloudless Server/Client)

- **One** shop books file per install. Server Mode: create if none, else open that one.
- **No** DeviceSetup create-new / open-list / remove-server picker.
- **No** `create_local_server` when a registry row already exists.
- Multi-outlet offline = separate device or OS user (separate data dir), not a second registry entry.
- Owner wipe: Settings → Backup → Delete local data (trading / schema / ui + Owner PIN) — same categories as Windows uninstall (`uninstall_wipe`, `delete-books-data.ps1`).
- **Emergency unlock PIN (duress)** is **offline cloudless LAN only** (not a cloud-account feature) and must keep working: `try_duress_unlock` → `wipe_trading_data_keep_structure` — wipe sales/ledgers/history only; **keep** menu, prices, tables, staff, settings, schema; open as Owner looking normal. Do not remove Team UI, unlock check order, or that wipe helper when changing Backup wipe.

## Cloud (later)

Multi-server / multi-shop on one account may return with cloud — **not** in the offline LAN path.

```text
❌ picking_server = true / show server_pick_section offline
❌ Create new server when one already exists
❌ Remove server from a DeviceSetup list
❌ Document “several local servers on one device” for offline LAN

✅ begin_server_mode → offline_server_id / create once
✅ Wipe shop setup returns to DeviceSetup
✅ Duplicate the same contract in Khaynjo and Moklanjo (no shared core)
```
